{"paper": "SSC-DelhiPoliceHC-20-Oct-2022-Shift3.pdf", "status": "ok", "mode": "sequential", "splitter": "qdot", "section_slice": true, "extracted_count": 20, "tagged_count": 20, "questions": [{"n": 1, "text": "", "options": [{"text": "970", "added": false}, {"text": "1030", "added": false}, {"text": "930", "added": false}, {"text": "900", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": true, "topic": "Algebra", "sub": "expression-values", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 2, "text": "A and B together can do a piece of work in 18 days. B and C together can do the same work in 24 days and A and C together can do the same work in 27 days. In how many days will A, B and C complete the entire work, working together?", "options": [], "options_source": "missing", "image_only": false, "topic": "Time-Work", "sub": "together-apart", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 3, "text": "", "options": [], "options_source": "missing", "image_only": true, "topic": "Number System", "sub": "fractions-decimals", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 4, "text": "What is the average of the first ten odd prime numbers?", "options": [{"text": "13.1", "added": false}, {"text": "15.8", "added": false}, {"text": "16.2", "added": false}, {"text": "12.9", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Average", "sub": "simple-average", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 5, "text": "Find the third proportional of 0.25 and 0.45.", "options": [{"text": "0.61", "added": false}, {"text": "0.81", "added": false}, {"text": "0.15", "added": false}, {"text": "0.35", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Ratio-Proportion", "sub": "proportion", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 6, "text": "If tan⁡θ + cot⁡θ = -2 , then the value of tan9θ + cot9θ is:", "options": [{"text": "2", "added": false}, {"text": "-1", "added": false}, {"text": "-2", "added": false}, {"text": "0", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Trigonometry", "sub": "identities", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 7, "text": "A conical tent is 48 m high and the diameter of its base is 28 m. What is the cost of canvas at the rate of Rs.80/m2 to make the tent?", "options": [{"text": "Rs. 1,80,000", "added": false}, {"text": "Rs. 1,76,000", "added": false}, {"text": "Rs. 1,96,000", "added": false}, {"text": "Rs. 1,48,000", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Mensuration 3D", "sub": "cone", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 8, "text": "", "options": [], "options_source": "missing", "image_only": true, "topic": "Simplification", "sub": "bodmas", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 9, "text": "If 35% of 60% of A is equal to 25% of 75% of B, then what is the ratio of A to B?", "options": [{"text": "25 : 28", "added": false}, {"text": "7 : 12", "added": false}, {"text": "12 : 7", "added": false}, {"text": "28 : 25", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Percentage", "sub": "basic-percentage", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 10, "text": "If Mohit covers three equal distances at the speed of 30 km/h, 25 km/h, and 20 km/h, respectively, then find his average speed during the whole journey.", "options": [{"text": "34.50 km/h", "added": false}, {"text": "24.32 km/h", "added": false}, {"text": "25.30 km/h @Qmaths", "added": false}, {"text": "43.32 km/h", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Time-Speed-Distance", "sub": "average-speed", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 11, "text": "In a boutique there are two workers and one machine to do the work of weaving. Shikha can finish the work in 10 hours on the machine, while Ruchika can finish it in 15 hours. Both workers Shikha and Ruchika work for an hour on alternate basis. In how many hours will the work be completed, if Shikha starts the work?", "options": [], "options_source": "missing", "image_only": false, "topic": "Time-Work", "sub": "alternate-days", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 12, "text": "If 3x − 7y = 10 and xy = −1, find the value of 9x2 + 49y2.", "options": [{"text": "71", "added": false}, {"text": "58", "added": false}, {"text": "63", "added": false}, {"text": "46", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Algebra", "sub": "identities", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 13, "text": "", "options": [{"text": "265", "added": false}, {"text": "269", "added": false}, {"text": "268", "added": false}, {"text": "260", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": true, "topic": "Data Interpretation", "sub": "table", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 14, "text": "If the simple interest on a sum of Rs.P at 5% per annum for three years is thrice the simple interest received on Rs.Q at 7% per annum for four years, then find the relation between P and Q.", "options": [{"text": "Q = 2.1P", "added": false}, {"text": "Q = 3.1P", "added": false}, {"text": "P = 4.8Q", "added": false}, {"text": "P = 5.6Q", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Simple Interest", "sub": "si-formula", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 15, "text": "When sold at a marked price, the product yields a profit of 25%. If the shopkeeper sells the product after providing a 20% discount on the marked price. Determine the net percentage profit earned by the shopkeeper.", "options": [{"text": "3%", "added": false}, {"text": "5%", "added": false}, {"text": "0%", "added": false}, {"text": "2%", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Discount", "sub": "mp-sp-relation", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 16, "text": "A dishonest shopkeeper sells sugar at ₹20 per kg which he bought at ₹15 per kg. Also, he gives 850 gm instead of 1000 gm. His actual profit or loss percentage is:", "options": [{"text": "45.45% profit", "added": false}, {"text": "42.56% loss", "added": false}, {"text": "50.12% loss", "added": false}, {"text": "56.86% profit", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Profit-Loss", "sub": "dishonest-dealer", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 17, "text": "", "options": [], "options_source": "missing", "image_only": true, "topic": "HCF-LCM", "sub": "hcf-lcm-of-numbers", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 18, "text": "A student wants to know the area of a rhombus, one of whose diagonals is 6 cm. He measures another diagonal as 8 cm. What is the area of the rhombus?", "options": [{"text": "48 cm2 @Qmaths", "added": false}, {"text": "25 cm2", "added": false}, {"text": "20 cm2", "added": false}, {"text": "24 cm2", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Mensuration 2D", "sub": "triangle-and-quadrilaterals", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 19, "text": "In ∆PQR, ∠P = 80°,∠Q = 58°, OQ and OR are the bisectors of ∠Q and ∠R, respectively. Find the value of ∠QOR.", "options": [{"text": "90°", "added": false}, {"text": "80°", "added": false}, {"text": "110°", "added": false}, {"text": "130°", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Geometry", "sub": "triangles", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 20, "text": "A money - lender borrows money at 6% per annum and pays the interest at the end of the year. He lends it at 8% per annum compound interest compounded half-yearly and receives the interest at the end of the year. In this way, he gains Rs.108 a year. The amount of money he borrows, is:", "options": [{"text": "Rs.6,000", "added": false}, {"text": "Rs.5,000", "added": false}, {"text": "Rs.5,500", "added": false}, {"text": "Rs.4,500", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Mixed / Composite", "sub": "two-topic-composite", "key_answer": null}]}